  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1215 AM CDT Thu Jul 23 2026\n\nHigh pressure slides across the Great Lakes into the Upper Ohio\nValley by week's end. This keeps a nice, cool northeasterly\nfetch here, providing lower dew points and temperatures through\nFriday; comfortably pleasant, especially for this time of year.\n\nWith the high's eastward shift, we get into return flow\nsoutherlies that bring our next chance of showers/storms heading\ninto the weekend. Locally heavy downpours look to be the main\nexpectation at this writing, as PW's push 2\". \n\nUpper level ridging takes over early next week, returning steamy\nheat that pushes headline numbers with triple digit heat indices\nand air temperatures approaching the century mark Monday and\nTuesday.",
